### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### API CACHING STRATEGIES — Workshop HTTP Requests
###
### Prerequisites:
###   1. Run `pnpm docker:up` (starts PostgreSQL + Redis)
###   2. Run `pnpm db:push` (push schema to DB)
###   3. Run `pnpm db:seed` (populates 6 events)
###   4. Run `pnpm start:dev` (starts the API on port 8000)
###
### Each response includes a `cache` object:
###   { strategy, key, hit, ttlMs }
### Watch `hit: true/false` to observe caching behavior in real time.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@host = http://localhost:8000
@contentType = application/json

# Paste an event id from a response below (seed data generates UUIDs at runtime)
@eventId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 1: Cache-Aside (Lazy Loading) — Read Path
###
### Pattern: check cache → if miss, query DB → store in cache → return
### Run the same request twice — first response has `hit: false` (cache miss),
### second response has `hit: true` (served from Redis, no DB query).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1a. List all events — FIRST call is a cache MISS (hits the database)
GET {{host}}/events

### 1b. List all events — SECOND call is a cache HIT (served from Redis)
###     Notice: same response, but hit: true and much faster
GET {{host}}/events

### 1c. Single event detail — demonstrates per-item caching (separate TTL)
###     Replace the UUID with a real id from the list response above
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 2: Versioned Cache Keys — How Filters Produce Unique Keys
###
### Each unique combination of query params generates a different cache key.
### The key also embeds a "list version" number for invalidation (see Lesson 3).
### Compare the `cache.key` values across these responses.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 2a. Filter by category — only webinars (2 seed events: Redis webinar + Caching Strategies)
GET {{host}}/events?category=webinar

### 2b. Filter by status — only published events (4 seed events)
GET {{host}}/events?status=published

### 2c. Filter virtual events only (2 seed events are virtual)
GET {{host}}/events?isVirtual=true

### 2d. Filter upcoming events (startsAt > now)
GET {{host}}/events?upcoming=true

### 2e. Search across title/location/organizer — e.g. "redis"
GET {{host}}/events?search=redis

### 2f. Pagination — page 1 with 2 items per page
GET {{host}}/events?page=1&pageSize=2

### 2g. Pagination — page 2 (different cache key, different data)
GET {{host}}/events?page=2&pageSize=2

### 2h. Sort by title descending
GET {{host}}/events?sortBy=title&sortOrder=desc

### 2i. Combined filters — webinars + published + sorted by startsAt
GET {{host}}/events?category=webinar&status=published&sortBy=startsAt&sortOrder=asc


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 3: Cache Invalidation — Version Bumping on Writes
###
### Strategy: Instead of scanning Redis for all cached list keys, we increment
### a version counter. List keys embed the version, so after a bump all old
### keys become unreachable (stale until TTL expiry, but never served).
###
### Steps to observe:
###   1. Run "List all events" (Lesson 1a) — note cache.key has version N
###   2. Run "Create" below — this bumps the version to N+1
###   3. Run "List all events" again — cache.key now has version N+1, hit: false
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 3a. Create a new event — triggers bumpListVersion()
# @name createEvent
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Cache Invalidation Workshop",
  "slug": "cache-invalidation-workshop",
  "description": "Live demo of version-based cache invalidation in NestJS APIs.",
  "location": "Nairobi Garage",
  "organizer": "KDP User Group",
  "category": "workshop",
  "status": "published",
  "startsAt": "2026-08-01T09:00:00+03:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-08-01T13:00:00+03:00",
  "capacity": 40,
  "isVirtual": false
}

### 3b. Now list events again — version bumped, so this is a cache MISS
###     Compare cache.key with the one from Lesson 1a — version number changed!
GET {{host}}/events


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 4: Detail Cache Invalidation — Explicit Key Deletion
###
### When you update or delete a specific event:
###   - The detail cache key for that item is explicitly deleted
###   - The list version is also bumped (since lists include the item)
###
### Steps:
###   1. GET an event by id — stores it in detail cache
###   2. PATCH the event — deletes the detail cache key + bumps list version
###   3. GET the same event — cache MISS (fresh data from DB)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 4a. Fetch a specific event — first call populates the detail cache
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### 4b. Update it — this invalidates both detail cache AND list version
PATCH {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "NestJS API Performance Clinic — UPDATED",
  "capacity": 80
}

### 4c. Fetch the same event — cache MISS, returns fresh updated data
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### 4d. Update status — another invalidation cycle
PATCH {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "cancelled"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 5: TTL (Time-To-Live) — Automatic Expiry
###
### Even without writes, cache entries expire after their TTL:
###   - List cache:    60s  (CACHE_TTL_MS)
###   - Detail cache:  120s (CACHE_DETAIL_TTL_MS)
###   - Version key:   24h  (CACHE_VERSION_TTL_MS)
###
### Exercise: Run a list request, wait 60+ seconds, run it again — hit: false.
### The cache expired naturally without any write operation.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 5a. Run this, wait 60 seconds, run it again to observe TTL expiry
GET {{host}}/events?category=workshop


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LESSON 6: Delete — Full Invalidation Cycle
###
### Deleting an event:
###   - Removes the detail cache key (event:{id})
###   - Bumps the list version (all list caches become stale)
###   - Returns 204 No Content
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 6a. Delete an event (expects 204 No Content)
DELETE {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### 6b. Confirm it's gone (expects 404 Not Found)
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### 6c. List events — cache MISS because version was bumped by the delete
GET {{host}}/events


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ERROR CASES — Validation & Conflict Handling
### (These don't affect the cache but demonstrate schema validation)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Duplicate slug (expects 409 Conflict)
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Duplicate Slug Test",
  "slug": "nestjs-api-performance-clinic",
  "location": "Nairobi",
  "organizer": "Test",
  "category": "meetup",
  "startsAt": "2026-09-01T09:00:00+03:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-09-01T17:00:00+03:00"
}

### Invalid payload — missing required fields (expects 400)
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "AB",
  "slug": "INVALID SLUG!"
}

### endsAt before startsAt (expects 400 — refinement validation)
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Bad Dates Event",
  "slug": "bad-dates-event",
  "location": "Nairobi",
  "organizer": "Test",
  "category": "meetup",
  "startsAt": "2026-09-15T17:00:00+03:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-09-15T09:00:00+03:00"
}

### Unknown field in update — strict schema rejects it (expects 400)
PATCH {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "price": 100
}

### Invalid UUID format (expects 400)
GET {{host}}/events/not-a-uuid

### Non-existent UUID (expects 404)
GET {{host}}/events/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000999

### Invalid sortBy field (expects 400)
GET {{host}}/events?sortBy=password

### pageSize over the max of 100 (expects 400)
GET {{host}}/events?pageSize=500
